          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Demonstrate the Tyndall effect using different colloids. Create a series of experiments showcasing how light scatters in colloids making the beam visible. Use laser pointers ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Safety first:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Use it under the supervision of an adult), flashlights, or other light sources for your demonstrations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.517,
            0.774,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Make crystals of different compounds (common salt, epsom salt, sugar, borax, nickel sulfate, etc.). Observe them under a magnifying glass or a microscope. Note down their colours and shapes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
